1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,678
Last episode we saw retrieval work.

2
00:00:01,678 --> 00:00:07,000
This time we open the hood — so you can predict when it will find the right passage, and when it quietly won't.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:07,495
Three steps.

4
00:00:07,495 --> 00:00:09,063
Every document gets split into chunks.

5
00:00:09,063 --> 00:00:11,210
Each chunk gets turned into a vector — an embedding.

6
00:00:11,210 --> 00:00:16,410
When you ask a question, the question is embedded too, and the app finds the nearest chunks by meaning, not by matching words.

7
00:00:16,410 --> 00:00:20,000
That's why asking about undoing a deploy finds a document about rolling back a release.

8
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,297
Three structural limits, not bugs.

9
00:00:21,297 --> 00:00:26,027
It's not exhaustive — it returns the nearest few chunks, not every relevant one, so a fact three chunks away can get missed.

10
00:00:26,027 --> 00:00:29,232
Chunk boundaries can split a sentence in half, separating a fact from its qualifier.

11
00:00:29,232 --> 00:00:34,000
And it matches meaning, not keywords, which is usually a strength but occasionally misses an exact term you needed literally.

12
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:35,319
A checklist for better answers.

13
00:00:35,319 --> 00:00:37,489
Use the documents' own vocabulary in your question.

14
00:00:37,489 --> 00:00:39,362
Ask narrow questions rather than broad ones.

15
00:00:39,362 --> 00:00:42,851
Explicitly ask it to say when something is absent, so it doesn't guess past a gap.

16
00:00:42,851 --> 00:00:44,766
Split unrelated material into separate bases.

17
00:00:44,766 --> 00:00:48,000
And name each base descriptively, so it's obvious later which one to attach.

18
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:52,074
The gotcha that catches people every time: a scanned PDF is just an image of text, not text.

19
00:00:52,074 --> 00:00:57,122
The app does no OCR, so indexing it silently succeeds and returns nothing useful — no error, just empty retrieval.

20
00:00:57,122 --> 00:01:00,000
If a document is a scan, run OCR on it yourself before adding it.

21
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,854
Knowledge grounds a chat in documents.

22
00:01:01,854 --> 00:01:06,000
Module 10 goes further — packaging a whole role, tools included, as a reusable agent.

